# Triply project rules

Triply is an explainable, situation-first destination recommender for domestic
tourism in Bangladesh. It is an academic project: methodology, explainability and
evaluation matter as much as features.

## Stack
- Vanilla HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript ES modules. No frameworks, no bundler, no build step.
- Backend (added in Phase 2): Supabase. Not before.
- Tests: node --test (package.json has "type": "module").

## Architecture rules
- The recommendation engine lives in js/engine/ as PURE functions: no DOM, no fetch,
  no globals. Everything is unit-tested.
- UI code lives in js/ui/. State lives in js/state.js. Data in data/destinations.json.
- All user-facing strings go through i18n (js/i18n/en.json, bn.json). Never hardcode text.
- All costs and travel times are estimates and must be labelled "estimate" in the UI.
- Every destination record has source and lastVerified. Never invent facts; if unknown,
  leave a clear TODO field.

## Code style
- Small modules, named exports, JSDoc on public functions, no dead code.
- CSS uses custom properties (design tokens) in css/tokens.css. Mobile-first.
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, keyboard navigation, visible focus, ARIA labels,
  sufficient contrast, prefers-reduced-motion respected.
- Work only on the current prompt's scope. Do not build ahead.
